LAST-MODIFIED:20260219T172136Z
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Kansas City (1996)
DTSTART:20260220T014500Z
DTEND:20260220T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T014500Z
UID:BtxkcMDG6T
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 128 mins (2h08m)\n\nJennifer Jason Leigh plays a Jea
 n Harlow-obsessed housewife who abducts the spouse of a local politician b
 efore the 1934 Democratic primary election. She goes on a wild ride\, and 
 so will you courtesy of Altman’s spirited recreations of the 1930s jazz 
 scene.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/kansas-city\n
 \nEstimated start: 18:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Round Midnight (1986)
DTSTART:20260220T044500Z
DTEND:20260220T072500Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T044500Z
UID:inxpsOBox0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 143 mins (2h23m)\n\nA troubled saxophonist (Dexter G
 ordon) cleans up his act in 1950s Paris\, but finds temptation lurking on 
 every street corner when he returns to reestablish his life in New York. C
 o-starring Herbie Hancock\, 1987 Academy Award winner Best Music\, Origina
 l Score for the film.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-cit
 y/round-midnight\n\nEstimated start: 21:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WKW: The Hand (2004)
DTSTART:20260221T012000Z
DTEND:20260221T024500Z
DTSTAMP:20260221T012000Z
UID:vwYjVBWqZ7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 66 mins (1h06m)\n\nWorld of Wong Kar Wai Like In the
  Mood for Love\, The Hand is set in the hazy Hong Kong of the 1960s\, but 
 its characters couldn’t be more different from the earlier film’s rest
 rained\, haunted lovers. Presented in its extended cut.\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/programs-and-events/world-of-wong-kar-wai/world-of-wong-kar-wai-the-
 hand\n\nEstimated start: 17:35
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WKW: In the Mood for Love (2000)
DTSTART:20260221T033000Z
DTEND:20260221T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20260221T033000Z
UID:JrmVxm9KhF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 117 mins (1h57m)\n\nWorld of Wong Kar Wai With its a
 ching musical soundtrack and exquisitely abstract cinematography by Christ
 opher Doyle and Mark Lee Ping-bin\, this film has been a major stylistic i
 nfluence on the past decade of cinema\, and is a milestone in Wong’s red
 oubtable career. Presented in 4K. The 25th Anniversary Edition includes I
 n the Mood for Love 2001\, a rarely-screened 9-minute short film that wil
 l play after the feature.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/worl
 d-of-wong-kar-wai/world-of-wong-kar-wai-in-the-mood-for-love\n\nEstimated 
 start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WKW: 2046 (2004)
DTSTART:20260221T230000Z
DTEND:20260222T013500Z
DTSTAMP:20260221T230000Z
UID:HwZl0lyu8s
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 139 mins (2h19m)\n\nWorld of Wong Kar Wai Several wo
 men enter a science fiction author's life over the course of a few years\,
  after the author has lost the woman he considers his one true love. Recog
 nized as the final film in Wong Kar-Wai's informal love trilogy\, preceded
  by Days of Being Wild (1990) and In the Mood for Love (2000). 4K resto
 ration.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/world-of-wong-kar-wai/
 world-of-wong-kar-wai-2046\n\nEstimated start: 15:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WKW: Happy Together (1997)
DTSTART:20260222T021500Z
DTEND:20260222T042000Z
DTSTAMP:20260222T021500Z
UID:SBYyb2MgWr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nWorld of Wong Kar Wai One of the
  most searing romances of the 1990s\, Wong Kar Wai’s emotionally raw\, l
 ushly stylized portrait of a relationship in breakdown casts Hong Kong sup
 erstars Tony Leung and Leslie Cheung as a couple traveling through Argenti
 na and locked in a turbulent cycle of infatuation and destructive jealousy
  as they break up\, make up\, and fall apart again and again. Presented i
 n 4K.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/world-of-wong-kar-wai/wo
 rld-of-wong-kar-wai-happy-together\n\nEstimated start: 18:30
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WKW: Chungking Express (1994)
DTSTART:20260222T050000Z
DTEND:20260222T071000Z
DTSTAMP:20260222T050000Z
UID:D4nA4ieOG9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nWorld of Wong Kar Wai Two hearts
 ick Hong Kong cops cross paths at the Midnight Express take-out restaurant
  stand\, where the ethereal pixie waitress Faye works. The whiplash\, doub
 le-pronged Chungking Express is one of the defining works of nineties cine
 ma and the film that made Hong Kong filmmaker Wong Kar Wai an instant icon
 . Presented in 4K.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/world-of-w
 ong-kar-wai/world-of-wong-kar-wai-chungking-express\n\nEstimated start: 21
 :15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wiz (1978)
DTSTART:20260222T200000Z
DTEND:20260222T225000Z
DTSTAMP:20260222T200000Z
UID:o1SuO88x6P
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 154 mins (2h34m)\n\nSliding Scale Community Screenin
 gs When Harlem schoolteacher Dorothy (Diana Ross) tries to save her dog fr
 om a storm\, she's miraculously whisked away to an urban fantasy land call
 ed Oz. This dazzling soul spectacular from legendary director Sidney Lumet
  reframes a beloved tale through the Black American experience\, creating 
 a powerful celebration of self-determination. New 4K restoration. In appre
 ciation of our movie-loving community\, tickets to this screening are avai
 lable on a sliding scale basis\, starting at $5 for child tickets. Enjoy t
 he film for less or give more generously to support nonprofit movie magic.
 \n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/sliding-scale-community-scree
 nings/the-wiz\n\nEstimated start: 12:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
